 "description": "A grass clearing cut by a winding dirt path, with a rounded clearing and a grass island inside it — the island is there because it is the only shape that exercises all four inner-corner masks at once, so the map doubles as a visual check that the 47-mask set is complete.",
 "cellSize": 16,
 "cols": 24,
 "rows": 14,
 "howToUse": "Every entry in `ground` and `props` is a tile id from this pack's tiles.json, so this map can be rebuilt in any engine: paint `ground` row by row (it is [row][col], top-left origin), then place `props` IN ORDER — later props may overlap earlier ones, which is deliberate (a bush in front of a tree), so the order is part of the data and not an incidental detail. `legend` lists only the tiles this map actually uses, so you can find them without hunting through the whole pack. An id written as `other-pack-id:tile_id` comes from a DIFFERENT pack — every one of those is listed in `requires`, so you can see at a glance what this map needs beyond this pack.",
